wb-cli (1.5.3) stable; urgency=medium

  Documentation rot — README and wiren-board skill still referenced
  state from before the 1.0/1.2/1.5 changes.

  * README: command table mentioned the removed ``modbus`` group;
    replaced with the actual ``serial wb-scan|templates|template|ports|
    device-info|device-params|device-set|devices|add-devices|send``
    surface that has been in place since 1.2.0. Added the new
    ``mqtt-debug enable|disable|status|capture`` row.
  * README: "Output modes" section claimed wb-cli picks JSON vs human
    via ``stdout.isatty()`` — this stopped being true in 1.0 (default
    is now always ``human``, JSON only via ``--json`` or
    ``WB_CLI_OUTPUT=json``). Section rewritten to match the actual
    behaviour and explain why.
  * README: source-tree snippet referenced ``commands/modbus/`` as the
    only subpackage and omitted the new ``lib/`` modules
    (``mqtt_log``, ``serial_conf``, ``serial_port``, ``modbus_crc``,
    ``modbus_frame``, ``templates``) and ``commands/serial/`` split
    (``_register / _scan / _add / _actions / _plugin``).
  * skills/wiren-board: "Common entry points" list missed
    ``mqtt-debug`` and ``cloud``. Added both.

  * serial wb-scan: removed the ``/dev/ttyMOD*`` filter that excluded
    those paths from multi-port scans. The filter assumed every
    ``ttyMOD*`` is a cellular modem, but installs that route RS-485
    through USB adapters or WBE2R modules wire those devices into
    ``wb-mqtt-serial.conf`` and the driver opens them just like
    ``/dev/ttyRS485-N``. ``wb-mqtt-serial/ports/Load`` is now the
    only source of truth — if the driver serves a port, the scan
    follows; if it doesn't, we don't second-guess. ``serial ports``
    and ``serial wb-scan`` iterate the same list.

  * skills/wb-serial: the "active ports" paragraph now notes that the
    driver's view is authoritative and includes USB-RS485 / MOD-style
    paths when they're wired into the config.

