wb-cli (1.5.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * mqtt-debug capture: ``--topic`` and ``--source`` now accept multiple
    values via ``action="append"`` — OR-match across patterns. Topic
    patterns containing MQTT wildcards ``+`` (one level) or ``#`` (zero
    or more remaining levels) are matched level-aware:
    ``--topic '/devices/+/controls/Channel 1 Dimming Level/on'`` and
    ``--topic '/devices/wb-mr6c_2/#'`` both work. Values without
    wildcards remain plain substring matches (grep-style) so simple
    ``--topic K1`` keeps working.
  * Background job's generated command now shell-quotes every
    ``--topic`` / ``--source`` / ``--output`` value via ``shlex.quote``
    so topics with spaces survive the round-trip through
    ``wb-cli job run "…"``.
  * mqtt-debug help: every example in the epilog explicitly quotes
    topics with spaces (``'Dimming Level'``, ``'Channel 1 …'``) and
    shows the SSH double-quoting trick. New examples cover multiple
    ``--topic`` flags, MQTT-wildcard patterns, and the SSH form.
  * Envelope shape: ``topic_filter`` / ``source_filter`` (scalars)
    replaced by ``topic_filters`` / ``source_filters`` (lists of
    strings) so LLMs can read what the capture actually filtered on.
  * 7 new tests on the parser side (multi-pattern, wildcards, topics
    with spaces, sources OR-match) + 2 new plugin tests. 283 total.

