wb-cli (1.5.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * New plugin ``mqtt-debug`` — verbose mosquitto PUBLISH tracing.
    Toggles ``log_type all`` via a drop-in
    ``/etc/mosquitto/conf.d/debug-verbose.conf``, parses
    ``Received PUBLISH …`` lines out of the journal into structured
    records (``source``, ``topic``, ``qos``, ``retain``, ``dup``,
    ``message_id``, ``payload_size``, ``timestamp``).
    Subcommands: ``enable`` / ``disable`` / ``status`` /
    ``capture --seconds N``. Inline up to 600 s with a countdown;
    longer captures (hours / days) require ``--background --output PATH``
    and run through ``wb-cli job run``. Previous on/off state is
    restored automatically via try/finally (skip with
    ``--keep-enabled``). Replaces the hand-rolled
    ``edit conf.d + restart + grep journal`` recipe with a single
    structured command suitable for both humans and LLMs.
    New ``wb_cli.lib.mqtt_log`` module for parsing PUBLISH lines —
    7 unit tests for the parser, 15 for the plugin.
  * skills/wb-mqtt-broker: new section "Verbose PUBLISH tracing —
    ``wb-cli mqtt-debug``" with the canonical commands, JSON shape, and
    a table of common ``source`` patterns (wb-rules, wb-mqtt-homeui,
    wb-modbus, tasmota_*, etc.).
  * serial wb-scan: the ``add_hint`` string became an ``add_hints``
    list. Every scan that found devices now offers both the "all
    ports at once" form (``wb-cli serial add-devices``) and the
    explicit ``--port`` per-port forms. Human output prints them as
    a block so users see both options without having to know about
    the 1.4.1 multi-port behaviour.

