wb-cli (1.4.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial wb-scan: at the end of a scan, wb-device-manager publishes a
    reset state (``scanning=false, progress=0, devices=[]``). The
    on_state handler used to swallow that message unconditionally,
    wiping the accumulated devices list and progress value right before
    declaring the scan complete. In single-port runs the symptom was a
    confusing ``TIMEOUT at 0%`` title; in multi-port runs whole ports'
    worth of devices were lost (8+2 found in progress → 8 reported).
    The handler now keeps the previous non-empty devices list and
    non-zero progress when the incoming message is the reset.
    Regression test added (``test_wb_scan_keeps_devices_through_reset_state``).
  * serial wb-scan (human): added a ``device_type`` column mirroring the
    one in ``serial devices``. wb-device-manager fills it
    (``configured_device_type``) when it matched a scan entry to an
    existing config row. The bus-side ``signature`` is still shown in
    its own column. Together the two columns let a user — or an LLM —
    cross-reference the scan and config tables on the same name
    rather than guessing whether ``WBMR3`` is the same device as
    ``WB-MR3``.

