wb-cli (1.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Plugin registry: ``serial`` is now addressed as ``wb_cli.commands.serial``
    just like every other command. The previously visible
    ``wb_cli.commands.serial._plugin`` suffix was an artefact of ``serial``
    being a package; ``_gen_registry`` now imports the package itself and the
    package re-exports ``PLUGIN`` from its ``__init__``. No user-visible change
    to ``wb-cli serial …`` calls.
  * lib/templates.py: new shared module for filesystem template lookup
    (``list_template_names``, ``read_template``, ``find_template_by_field``,
    ``find_template``). Custom templates in ``/etc/wb-mqtt-serial.conf.d/templates``
    win over packaged ones, ``deprecated`` paths are deprioritised. ``serial
    templates`` / ``serial template`` / ``serial add-devices`` no longer shell
    out to ``find``/``cat``/``grep`` — all template I/O goes through the lib
    layer.
  * skills/wiren-board: replaced removed ``modbus`` group with ``serial`` /
    ``serial-debug`` in the entry-point list; "Quick diagnostic sequence" now
    relies on ``wb-cli audit`` instead of duplicating ``systemctl --failed``.
  * skills/wb-serial: moved the ``wb-cli serial …`` shortcuts to the top of
    the skill and demoted the raw MQTT-RPC base pattern to a fallback. Bus
    scan and debug-collection sections now drive the flow through
    ``wb-cli serial wb-scan`` and ``wb-cli serial-debug`` (with
    ``wb-cli job run`` for long captures); raw ``bus-scan/Start`` and the
    sed-and-restart script are kept only as fallbacks.

 -- Alexander Degtyarev <a.degtyarev@wirenboard.com>  Wed, 13 May 2026 10:34:07 +0400

wb-cli (1.2.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial ports / serial wb-scan: always go through wb-mqtt-serial RPCs
    instead of reading /etc/wb-mqtt-serial.conf directly. An empty result
    is now a signalled error (driver dropped its config — usually schema
    validation) with a hint pointing at `wb-cli confed load/save` and the
    wb-mqtt-serial journal. The previous fallback into the raw JSON file
    silently hid those failures from the user.
  * serial wb-scan hint when no ports: explicit suggestion to repair the
    config via confed RPC, plus `--port /dev/ttyRS485-N` as a bypass for
    scanning an unconfigured port without enumerating.
  * serial wb-scan hint on per-port-failure timeout: mention --bootloader
    alongside --slow.

 -- Alexander Degtyarev <a.degtyarev@wirenboard.com>  Wed, 13 May 2026 05:30:00 +0300

wb-cli (1.2.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial wb-scan: pass `port` to wb-device-manager as a dict with UART
    params, not a bare string — wb-device-manager silently ignored the
    string form, so `--port /dev/ttyRS485-N` scans returned 0 devices.
  * serial wb-scan: detect completion via the `scanning=true→false`
    transition wb-device-manager publishes at end-of-scan instead of
    timing out after `progress=100`. The old logic reset the wait window
    on the post-scan `progress=0` state and never declared the scan done.
  * serial wb-scan (no --port): iterate over RS-485 ports from
    /etc/wb-mqtt-serial.conf and scan each one. wb-mqtt-serial/ports/Load
    is no longer used — it returns empty when any port stanza fails
    schema validation, which silently hid bus devices. `/dev/ttyMOD*`
    (cellular modem ports) are skipped.
  * serial wb-scan: continue past per-port failures — wb-device-manager's
    `error` field is reported in `failed_ports` instead of aborting the
    whole multi-port run.

